codex
A security anomaly changes the libssh2 baseline: released `1.11.1` is not clean as of this audit. Upstream has an open request for `1.11.2` to ship the fix for CVE-2026-7598, plus a June 2026 AEAD uninitialized-memory disclosure report. I’m checking whether the pinned candidate must move from the release tag to an exact post-fix upstream commit; I will not silently bless a vulnerable release.
