ISSUE2023
{
  "number": 2023,
  "title": "AEAD ciphers (chacha20-poly1305, AES-GCM) leak 16 bytes of uninitialized memory per outgoing encrypted packet",
  "state": "open",
  "body": "## Description\n\nWhen using AEAD ciphers (`chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com` or `aes*-gcm@openssh.com`), the `total_length` calculation in `_libssh2_transport_send()` (`transport.c`, line 1158-1161) double-counts `mac_len` and `auth_len`, causing 16 bytes of uninitialized heap memory to be sent with every encrypted outgoing packet.\n\n## Root Cause\n\n### Bug A: `_libssh2_mac_override()` does not cover chacha20-poly1305\n\n`mac.c:501-512` — For AES-GCM, the function returns a stub MAC (`mac_method_hmac_aesgcm`, mac_len=16) that causes the separate MAC computation to be skipped via the `INTEGRATED_MAC` flag. But for chacha20-poly1305, it returns `NULL`, so the separately negotiated HMAC (e.g., hmac-sha2-256, mac_len=32) remains active. This causes a 32-byte HMAC to be computed and written to the output buffer, even though chacha20-poly1305 already has its own 16-byte Poly1305 auth tag.\n\n### Bug B: `total_length` double-counts mac_len + auth_len\n\n`transport.c:1158-1161`:\n```c\ntotal_length = packet_length + (encrypted && local_mac ? local_mac->mac_len : 0);\ntotal_length += auth_len;\n```\n\nFor chacha20-poly1305 with hmac-sha2-256:\n- `total_length = packet_length + 32 (HMAC) + 16 (Poly1305) = packet_length + 48`\n- But only `packet_length + 32` bytes are actually written (packet + 32 bytes of auth data)\n- **16 bytes at `outbuf[packet_length+32..packet_length+47]` are uninitialized**\n\nFor AES-GCM:\n- `total_length = packet_length + 16 (stub MAC) + 16 (GCM tag) = packet_length + 32`\n- But only `packet_length + 16` bytes are written (packet + 16-byte GCM tag)\n- **16 bytes at `outbuf[packet_length+16..packet_length+31]` are uninitialized**\n\n### Evidence: AES-GCM already caught by debug assert\n\n`transport.c:1247`:\n```c\nassert((size_t)total_length <=\n       packet_length + session->local.crypt->blocksize);\n// For AES-GCM: assert(packet_length + 32 <= packet_length + 16) → FALSE\n// This assert fires in debug builds but is a no-op in release builds (-DNDEBUG)\n```\n\n## Impact\n\n**CWE-200**: Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor\n\n- 16 bytes of uninitialized heap memory sent per encrypted outgoing packet\n- `outbuf` is `unsigned char outbuf[MAX_SSH_PACKET_LEN]` allocated via the user's allocator (typically `malloc`, not `calloc`)\n- Uninitialized memory may contain data from previous heap allocations (potentially keys, passwords, or other sensitive data)\n- The leaked bytes are encrypted (attacker needs session key to read them)\n- For chacha20-poly1305, the leaked 16 bytes are NOT covered by the Poly1305 authentication tag (can be modified without detection)\n\n## Arithmetic Verification\n\n```\nchacha20-poly1305 + hmac-sha2-256:\n  total_length = packet_length + 32 + 16 = packet_length + 48\n  bytes written = packet_length + 32 (packet + MAC hash + auth tag)\n  bytes sent = total_length = packet_length + 48\n  LEAKED: 16 bytes uninitialized\n\nAES-GCM:\n  total_length = packet_length + 16 + 16 = packet_length + 32\n  bytes written = packet_length + 16 (packet + GCM tag)\n  bytes sent = total_length = packet_length + 32\n  LEAKED: 16 bytes uninitialized\n```\n\n## Suggested Fix\n\nTwo changes needed:\n\n1. `mac.c:504-507` — Extend `_libssh2_mac_override()` to cover chacha20-poly1305:\n```c\nif(!strcmp(crypt->name, \"chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com\") ||\n   !strcmp(crypt->name, \"aes256-gcm@openssh.com\") ||\n   !strcmp(crypt->name, \"aes128-gcm@openssh.com\"))\n    return &mac_method_hmac_aesgcm;\n```\n\n2. `transport.c:1158-1161` — Fix `total_length` to not double-count for AEAD:\n```c\nif(CRYPT_FLAG_L(session, REQUIRES_FULL_PACKET) ||\n   CRYPT_FLAG_L(session, INTEGRATED_MAC))\n    total_length = packet_length + auth_len;\nelse\n    total_length = packet_length + (encrypted && local_mac ? local_mac->mac_len : 0);\n```\n\nDiscovered through code audit of the libssh2 1.11.2_DEV security surface.",
  "created_at": "2026-06-10T14:14:54Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-06-30T22:48:50Z",
