2026-06-15T16:22:00Z	willco007	We are working towards a release. This issue specifically doesn't carry any more risk than any other buffer overflow. If the server is compromised and sending you invalid user auth lists, they have your data already and that is a much more significant issue than a local OOB read which will crash the client.
2026-06-23T20:01:08Z	jayaddison	A few more vulnerabilities valid up-to-and-including v1.11.1 have been published; [CVE-2025-15661](https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2025-15661) and [CVE-2026-55199](https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-55199) and then [CVE-2026-55200](https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-55200) respectively.\n\nAs with CVE-2026-7598 (the vulnerability that this thread was reported against), commits/patches to resolve each of these are available, and I'll list them in the footer of this message.\n\nIf you are following this thread and believe that it is crucial that your environment resolves these, please consider asking your vendor to apply the patches as a security update -- or -- if you have the in-house ability, patch your vendor packages and distribute binary packages locally.\n\n(it is a design-goal of FOSS that you can rebuild, patch and distribute FOSS software yourself; upstream support for any software is not guaranteed to last forever -- having the complete source and means to build it is an escape hatch, and a practice that is worth learning, even though it is rarely needed)\n\nThe patch commit IDs are:\n\n- Firstly, to avoid an out-of-bounds read in some SFTP symlink code: [`2dae3024897e1898d389835151f4e9606227721d`](2dae3024897e1898d389835151f4e9606227721d)\n- Secondly, to prevent an infinite loop when parsing SSH info metadata during the pre-authentication phase: [`17626857d20b3c9a1addfa45979dadcee1cd84a4`](17626857d20b3c9a1addfa45979dadcee1cd84a4)\n- Thirdly, adding some additional out-of-bounds array checks -- I'm not sure whether an attack that exploits this would require an already-authenticated session: [`97acf3dfda80c91c3a8c9f2372546301d4a1a7a8`](97acf3dfda80c91c3a8c9f2372546301d4a1a7a8)\n\nWithout knowing whether an authenticated session is required for the third vulnerability, my initial sense would be that the second patch (preventing a pre-auth infinite loop) would be the most important to install on hosts that are SSH clients via `libssh2`, particularly if they interact with untrusted or semi-trusted SSH servers.
2026-06-25T11:05:42Z	dvzrv	Not to dogpile, but as a downstream maintainer I would like to 2nd the request for a new release.\nThe above mentioned commits don't apply cleanly, which means that they have to be backported manually.
2026-07-10T18:51:33Z	mbauman	As another downstream maintainer working to keep up here, there are (as of today) six CVEs tagged against [`libssh2:libssh2`](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/search#/nvd/home?cpeFilterMode=applicability&cpeName=cpe:2.3:a:libssh2:libssh2:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*&resultType=records) that affect v1.11.1:\n\nAdvisory | Patch | Details\n-- | -- | --\n[CVE-2026-7598](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-7598) | https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/commit/256d04b60d80bf1190e96b0ad1e91b2174d744b1  | commit named in the advisory\n[CVE-2026-58051](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-58051) | https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/commit/a9758da45a52bc8c630ec9493804d0c6ea30b24a | my best understanding\n[CVE-2026-58050](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-58050) | https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/commit/34497525929b9a47f03dfb81887ac896202b7e12 | my best understanding; requires renaming `ssh2_err` to its old `_libssh2_err` name)\n[CVE-2026-55200](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-55200) | https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/commit/97acf3dfda80c91c3a8c9f2372546301d4a1a7a8 | `7acf3df` named in the advisory (yes, missing the leading `9`)\n[CVE-2026-55199](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-55199) | https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/commit/17626857d20b3c9a1addfa45979dadcee1cd84a4 |  `1762685` named in the advisory\n[CVE-2025-15661](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-15661) | https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/commit/2dae3024897e1898d389835151f4e9606227721d |  `2dae302` named in the advisory, requires the `libssh2_priv.h` change from 606c102e52f8447de2b745dd6c5ddf418defc519\n\nDebian has back ported 4/6 of these thus far: https://udd.debian.org/patches.cgi?src=libssh2&version=1.11.1-4
