2026-06-23T21:24:54Z	willco007	I ran Claude on this issue (use AI against AI) and this is what it came up with:\n\n> The 16-byte uninitialized memory leak described in the issue does not exist in the current codebase. The reporter's analysis incorrectly assumed that both local_mac->mac_len and auth_len would be non-zero simultaneously for AEAD ciphers, but the if/else branch at line 1024–1028 ensures they are mutually exclusive. The real bug — which the patch does fix — is that a live HMAC was being computed and written into the output buffer for chacha20-poly1305 sessions, which is a correctness problem (corrupted output, potential interop failure) but not the specific memory leak described.\n\nI have created a patch to resolve that issue which I will submit soon after additional validation.
2026-06-30T22:48:50Z	willco007	Update to this, I need to step through this code and do in-depth debugging as both Claude and the above suggestions break certain algorithm combinations.
