codex
The macOS release build of the pinned SwiftNIO SSH source succeeded with the exact resolved dependency graph. I’ve also confirmed the two decisive source-level differences: SwiftNIO SSH hardcodes a 16 MiB child receive window and keeps client rekey internal; libssh2 exposes per-channel receive-window APIs but likewise has no public client-rekey trigger, so rekey remains a non-negotiable experiment for both.
